,137 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors**) both passed! Waiting for the Dart leg and browser `:demo` build to complete.\nFixed a CLJS `:infer-warning` on `FnArgRef/-equiv` in [reader.cljc](file:///home/sto/ci/datomworld-floatkind/src/cljc/yang/clojure/reader.cljc#L452-L468). Re-verifying the `:demo` build, Node 7-gates, and `clj-kondo` while the Dart leg completes.\n`clj-kondo` finished cleanly (**0 errors**, **0 warnings** in all r1/r2 edited files). Waiting for `:demo` + Node 7-gates and the Dart leg to complete.\nDart leg passed (**69/69 tests passed, 0 failures, 0 errors**). Browser `:demo` build passed with **0 warnings** (324 files), and Node 7-gates re-passed (**30 tests / 605 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors**) after the `FnArgRef` type-hint fix. Running a final post-hint Node REPL sanity check and gathering `git status` / timestamps before writing the r2 findings report.\nCompleted-GMT: 2026-11-26 17:15:59 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-11-26 12:15:59 EST\n\nAll seven sign-off blockers (**B-1..B-7**) for `fix/float-kind-portability` r2 are resolved within RULING 5's file boundaries, verified with RED→GREEN TDD evidence across JVM, Node, Dart, and Jolt, and left uncommitted for the orchestrator.\n\n### Summary of Fixes\n- **B-1**: Preserved orchestrator commit `93f95f1c` (`(:require` opener restored in [clojure_float_kind_test.cljc](file:///home/sto/ci/datomworld-floatkind/test/yang/clojure_float_kind_test.cljc#L16)).\n- **B-2**: Replaced `if-let [x (first xs)]` truthiness loops with `reduce` in `build-checked-set` and `build-checked-map` ([reader.cljc](file:///home/sto/ci/datomworld-floatkind/src/cljc/yang/clojure/reader.cljc#L365-L387)) so `false`/`nil` elements and keys survive at every position and duplicate detection continues after them.\n- **B-3**: Replaced `if-let [nxt (first xs)]` with `(seq more)` sequence-presence testing in `clj-=` ([numeric.cljc](file:///home/sto/ci/datomworld-floatkind/src/cljc/yang/clojure/numeric.cljc#L177-L191)), fixing `(= 1 1 false) =\u003e false` and variadic `clj-!=` negation including operands after `false`/`nil`.\n- **B-4**: Eliminated the `::discard` value sentinel by separating parse control state (`[:discard nil end-i]` vs `[:value val end-i]`) across `read-form-1`, `read-form*`, `read-delimited`, `read-next-required`, and `read-forms` ([reader.cljc](file:///home/sto/ci/datomworld-floatkind/src/cljc/yang/clojure/reader.cljc#L345-L875)), preserving `:yang.clojure.reader/discard` and all guest literals in every position.\n- **B-5**: Replaced fixed `p__1`/`p__2`/`p__rest` anonymous-fn names with a parse-local unforgeable `FnArgRef` placeholder and post-parse `collect-used-syms` + `fresh-param-sym` (`p\u003ck\u003e__\u003cn\u003e#`, `rest__\u003cn\u003e#`) substitution ([reader.cljc](file:///home/sto/ci/datomworld-floatkind/src/cljc/yang/clojure/reader.cljc#L452-L575)), fixing the 4-vs-12 counterexample and all positional/rest colliding bindings with deterministic canonical output.\n- **B-6**: Removed `'` (`39`) from `macro-terminating?` ([reader.cljc](file:///home/sto/ci/datomworld-floatkind/src/cljc/yang/clojure/reader.cljc#L111-L129)), implemented portable scalar/collection syntax-quote `` ` `` preserving `numeric-carrier?` scalars, unquote `~`, unquote-splicing `~@`, deterministic `foo#` auto-gensym, and metadata ([reader.cljc](file:///home/sto/ci/datomworld-floatkind/src/cljc/yang/clojure/reader.cljc#L578-L705)), and restored `#^`, `#\u003c`, and `@x` → `(clojure.core/deref x)`, verified against `clojure.tools.reader`/`cljs.tools.reader` on a 33-case differential lexical corpus.\n- **B-7**: Added `gate5-pre-pause-integral-float-across-continuation-and-snapshot` ([clojure_float_kind_test.cljc](file:///home/sto/ci/datomworld-floatkind/test/yang/clojure_float_kind_test.cljc#L600-L703)) verifying integral floats computed **before** a continuation pause (`2.0` in VM store, `5.0` and `-0.0` in the lexical continuation frame) retain float64 kind, value, IEEE-754 bits, and canonical CBOR i